{"complete":true,"school_name":"Southwestern University","town_name":"Georgetown","boards":[{"complete":true,"school_name":"Southwestern University","town_name":"Georgetown","template_id":"college-blocks-off-campus","title":"10 Blocks Off Campus, One Reason Each","description":"Ten documented stops on Georgetown’s downtown walking-tour corridors, each with a distinct architectural or local-history detail to look for.","icon":"location_city","cards":[{"subject_id":"historic-williamson-county-courthouse","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Historic Williamson County Courthouse","title":"Historic Williamson County Courthouse: inspect the copper dome","subtitle":"Austin Avenue corridor, downtown Georgetown","notes":"Circle the courthouse grounds and look up at the copper dome, Ionic-columned porticoes, pediments, and balustrade described by the walking-tour record.","short_summary":"A 1911 Beaux Arts courthouse and the walking tour’s central civic landmark.","evidence_claim":"Preservation Georgetown identifies this 1911 C. H. Page-designed courthouse as the focal point of the central business district and documents its copper dome and Ionic porticoes.","source_url":"https://www.preservationgeorgetown.org/walk-this-way/2.-historic-williamson-county-courthouse","source_title":"Historic Williamson County Courthouse | Preservation Georgetown","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use the exterior grounds and follow posted access rules for the building.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"palace-theatre-1925","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Palace Theatre","title":"Palace Theatre: spot the Art Deco façade","subtitle":"Austin Avenue corridor, downtown Georgetown","notes":"Pause outside to photograph the flat and three-dimensional Art Deco motifs; check the theatre’s own schedule separately before planning a performance.","short_summary":"A 1925 theatre remodeled into its present Art Deco appearance in 1936.","evidence_claim":"Preservation Georgetown says the Palace was built in 1925, remodeled to its present Art Deco appearance in 1936, and rehabilitated as a community performing-arts center in the 1990s.","source_url":"https://www.preservationgeorgetown.org/walk-this-way/24.-palace-theatre-%281925%29","source_title":"Palace Theatre (1925) | Preservation Georgetown","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Exterior viewing is the reliable option; performance access depends on the theatre’s schedule and ticketing.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"steele-store-makemson-hotel","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Steele Store & Makemson Hotel","title":"Steele Store & Makemson Hotel: trace the early commercial corner","subtitle":"West 8th Street corridor, downtown Georgetown","notes":"Read the building as a layered corner: the record traces uses here from a hotel and stage stop to dry goods, banking, hotel, retail, and professional space.","short_summary":"A restored limestone commercial complex with documented uses reaching back to 1848.","evidence_claim":"Preservation Georgetown documents commercial activity at this corner from 1848 and says rehabilitation begun in 1981 helped inspire downtown Georgetown’s revitalization.","source_url":"https://www.preservationgeorgetown.org/walk-this-way/23.-steele-store-%26-makemson-hotel","source_title":"Steele Store & Makemson Hotel | Preservation Georgetown","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View the historic exterior from the public sidewalk; individual tenant access varies.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":