896%29","source_title":"M.B. Lockett Building (1896) | Preservation Georgetown","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Exterior architectural viewing from the public sidewalk is appropriate; tenant access varies.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"fire-house-old-city-hall","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Fire House and Old City Hall","title":"Fire House and Old City Hall: locate the original fire bell","subtitle":"South Main Street corridor, downtown Georgetown","notes":"Walk the building’s edge and look for the original fire bell above the pocket-park area, where the former water-tower footprint is documented.","short_summary":"An 1892 limestone civic building built for Georgetown’s volunteer fire department and municipal operations.","evidence_claim":"Preservation Georgetown says this 1892 structure housed the Hook and Ladder Company and municipal operations, and that the standpipe perimeter remains visible beneath the original fire bell.","source_url":"https://www.preservationgeorgetown.org/walk-this-way/42.-fire-house-and-old-city-hall-%281892%29","source_title":"Fire House and Old City Hall (1892) | Preservation Georgetown","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use the sidewalk and adjacent public pocket-park area; do not enter restricted portions.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"grace-heritage-center","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Grace Heritage Center","title":"Grace Heritage Center: photograph the Gothic details","subtitle":"South Main Street corridor, downtown Georgetown","notes":"From Founders Memorial Park, frame the pointed-arch and diamond-shaped windows, stained glass, and tower finials of this restored former sanctuary.","short_summary":"Georgetown’s oldest wood-frame religious structure, now preserved at its current downtown site.","evidence_claim":"Preservation Georgetown identifies Grace Heritage Center as the city’s oldest wood-frame religious structure and documents its Gothic Revival windows, stained glass, and tower detailing.","source_url":"https://www.preservationgeorgetown.org/walk-this-way/43.-grace-heritage-center-%281881%29","source_title":"Grace Heritage Center (1881) | Preservation Georgetown","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View the exterior and park setting; event or interior access is scheduled separately.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"old-us-post-office","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Old U.S. Post Office","title":"Old U.S. Post Office: add a federal-era façade to the walk","subtitle":"East 8th Street corridor, downtown Georgetown","notes":"Use the tour’s red QR markers to identify this 1931 stop, then compare its form with the neighboring older commercial buildings on the Square.","short_summary":"A named 1931 stop on Preservation Georgetown’s self-guided downtown route.","evidence_claim":"Preservation Georgetown lists the Old U.S. Post Office (1931) as a stop on its self-guided Downtown Walking Tour of the Square and nearby blocks.","source_url":"https://www.preservationgeorgetown.org/downtown-walking-tour","source_title":"Downtown Walking Tour | Preservation Georgetown","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Follow the self-guided tour from public sidewalks and scan any posted red QR marker.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"old-williamson-county-jail","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Old Williamson County Jail",