ary.","short_summary":"Georgetown’s oldest wood-frame religious structure, now preserved at its current downtown site.","evidence_claim":"Preservation Georgetown identifies Grace Heritage Center as the city’s oldest wood-frame religious structure and documents its Gothic Revival windows, stained glass, and tower detailing.","source_url":"https://www.preservationgeorgetown.org/walk-this-way/43.-grace-heritage-center-%281881%29","source_title":"Grace Heritage Center (1881) | Preservation Georgetown","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View the exterior and park setting; event or interior access is scheduled separately.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"old-us-post-office","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Old U.S. Post Office","title":"Old U.S. Post Office: add a federal-era façade to the walk","subtitle":"East 8th Street corridor, downtown Georgetown","notes":"Use the tour’s red QR markers to identify this 1931 stop, then compare its form with the neighboring older commercial buildings on the Square.","short_summary":"A named 1931 stop on Preservation Georgetown’s self-guided downtown route.","evidence_claim":"Preservation Georgetown lists the Old U.S. Post Office (1931) as a stop on its self-guided Downtown Walking Tour of the Square and nearby blocks.","source_url":"https://www.preservationgeorgetown.org/downtown-walking-tour","source_title":"Downtown Walking Tour | Preservation Georgetown","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Follow the self-guided tour from public sidewalks and scan any posted red QR marker.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"old-williamson-county-jail","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Old Williamson County Jail",